      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Pay and shares deal nearly matches $58m award to John Ternus, his successor as CEO at the $4.7tn tech company</p><p>Tim Cook has received a $47m (£35m) pay deal as Apple’s executive chair, a remuneration package that nears the level set for his successor as chief executive.</p><p>Cook, who handed over to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/20/john-ternus-apple-ceo-tim-cook\">John Ternus</a> on Tuesday, will be paid a base salary of $2m and <a href=\"https://d18rn0p25nwr6d.cloudfront.net/CIK-0000320193/267c15fa-d3b6-4b5b-9bd0-3b187635d9eb.pdf\">$45m worth of shares</a>. Half of the share award will be based on performance targets being met, while the remaining half will be paid out over four years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/02/tim-cook-47m-package-chair-apple\">Continue reading...</a>"
